# Lune

A browser built from spare parts. Used by [@leebyron](https://leebyron.com); you can use it too.

Lune is an open source Chromium browser for macOS, built on [ungoogled-chromium](https://github.com/ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium/) and [Helium](https://helium.computer/), with selected work from [Xelium](https://github.com/minervanet/xelium-macos) and interaction ideas inspired by [Arc](https://arc.net/).

- A vertical tab sidebar and toolbar that tuck away to give pages more room.
- A keyboard command menu: press **Cmd-T** to search, switch tabs, or run browser commands.
- Automatic Older Tabs to keep inactive tabs out of the way, with configurable retention.

Visit [lune.computer](https://lune.computer/) for a look at the browser.

## Download

Requires **macOS 13 or later**.

| Mac | Latest download |
| --- | --- |
| Apple silicon (M-series) | [Download Lune for Apple silicon](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/releases/latest/download/Lune-macos-arm64.dmg) |
| Intel | [Download Lune for Intel](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/releases/latest/download/Lune-macos-x86_64.dmg) |

Open the DMG and drag Lune to Applications. Releases are signed and notarized, and the browser can keep itself up to date through Lune's GitHub releases.

See the [latest release notes](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/releases/latest) or browse [all releases](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/releases).

Optional browser services are provided by Helium and require separate consent. Read Lune's [privacy policy](https://lune.computer/privacy) and [terms](https://lune.computer/terms) for details.

## About this repository

This repository holds Lune's source, build tooling, website, and published releases. The browser is assembled from Chromium and a set of patches; the full Chromium source tree is downloaded during source preparation.

The `main` branch contains product configuration, pinned build inputs in [manifests/](manifests/), build and release tooling in [scripts/](scripts/), and the [website](website/). Browser code and patches live on component branches that preserve their upstream histories:

- [component/helium](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/tree/component/helium): core browser patches and configuration.
- [component/macos](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/tree/component/macos): macOS patches, build tooling, and packaging.
- [component/services](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/tree/component/services): optional service source.

Each release tag records its source and exact build inputs. The [development lockfile](manifests/browser.lock.json) selects inputs for future builds; published releases retain their own frozen inputs.

Report bugs and suggest improvements in [Issues](https://github.com/leebyron/lune-browser/issues).

